  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "GSM A RR: Tell Coverity to ignore if a return is checked",
  "description": "The gsm_rr_csn_HL_flag usually indicates presence or absence of\nsomething in the frame, but sometimes indicates features that don't\nresult in changes in dissection. If Coverity notices that the return\nof a function is checked most of the time, and many times, it will\nwarn about it by default, as here.\n\nThe Coverity documentation is ambigious about whether this should be\nno_checked_return or no-checked-return (it uses one in one place and the\nother in another.)",
